> This is a different implementation than that from SporkHack?

Yes. It is different. The main reason I haven't posted the exact
details about it (or about some other things) is that I haven't
settled on exactly how it should work. Currently the conflict resist
check is this: rn2(level_difficulty()) >=3D u.ulevel-(int)mtmp->m_lev/2)
&& (the normal resistance check).
So for example, near the end of the game, level_difficulty ~ 50, m_lvl
~ 20, ulevel ~ 20.. this resistance is around 80%. But as I said, I'll
probably change it again before I'm happy with it. Maybe I should
bring CHA into it, like sporkhack does.

